OpenMUI [RELEASE] ([STAGE]) for AmigaOS 3.x / m68k
=================================================

OpenMUI is a free, open-source replacement for MUI on AmigaOS 3.x. It
provides muimaster.library, the built-in classes and a preferences
program, and runs programs written for MUI 3, 4 and 5. Its look and
memory use follow MUI 3.8.

OpenMUI is not MUI and is not affiliated with MUI's authors. MUI was
created by Stefan Stuntz; MUI 4 and 5 come from the MUI team. MUI was
studied black-box only: its behaviour was measured and its public
documentation read; its code was never read or copied.

Origins: Zune (The AROS Development Team), ported to AmigaOS 3 as Zune68
(Stefan Reinauer); OpenMUI is the lean edition of Zune68.

This is a public beta ([STAGE], [RELEASE]). All figures were measured in
an emulator (FS-UAE), not on a real Amiga.

